      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to understand this `while` loop and found out this CL. I doubted how this loop works. For example, with `HOOK_TICK_INTERVAL_MS` being 250ms, the linear transition sequence is like:\n```\n\tcolor-0 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026right_led_white\u003e;\n\t\tperiod-ms \u003d \u003c100\u003e;\n\t}\n\tcolor-1 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026right_led_amber\u003e;\n\t\tperiod-ms \u003d \u003c100\u003e;\n\t}\n\tcolor-2 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026right_led_white\u003e;\n\t\tperiod-ms \u003d \u003c200\u003e;\n\t}\n\tcolor-3 {\n\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026right_led_amber\u003e;\n\t\tperiod-ms \u003d \u003c200\u003e;\n\t}\n        ...\n```\n\nAt 0ms, the `color-0` is applied and the `cur_color` is advanced from `0` to `2`, because of the elapsed_ms calculation: 0 -\u003e +250ms -\u003e -100ms -\u003e -100ms -\u003e 50ms.\n\nAt 250ms (the next tick hook), `color-2` is applied. However, the `color-1` is never be applied. This is because at 0ms, `led_asynchronous_apply_color` only performs the transition for `color-0` and continues the transition even after 100ms (I am not sure if we have any boundary check). As a result, the transition for `color-1` is skipped. \n\nAnother problem is that the `color-2` timing is wrong, as its starts from 25% because elapsed_ms starts from 50ms instead 0ms, 50ms / 200ms \u003d 25%.\n\nI think we can\u0027t relax the restriction that `period-ms` must be a multiple of `HOOK_TICK_INTERVAL_MS`.",
